  "notes": "Opposite of いい/よい (good). {悪|わる}い is one of the most common adjectives. As a casual apology, {悪|わる}い or {悪|わる}いね is like saying 'my bad' or 'sorry about that'. More formal apology: すみません or ごめんなさい.",
